<title>POLAND: Polfa-K to sell plant to BASF.</title>
<headline>Polfa-K to sell plant to BASF.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish drug maker Polfa Kutno has signed an initial agreement with a Polish unit of German chemical concern BASF AG on selling it a veterinary drugs and food concentrates plant, Polfa said on Friday.</p>
<p>Polfa's deputy president Jan Krysiuk told Reuters that the plant Wytwornia Premiksow, based in the central city of Kutno, would be sold for more than 16 million zlotys.</p>
<p>&quot;The book value of the plant is about 16 million zlotys and the sale price is much higher than that...We are selling the factory because we want to focus on pharmaceuticals for people,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
